+## The Docker host check
+
+**Docker → Host** (`/machines/{id}/docker/host`, `machine.view`) shows
+how the Docker Engine is set up - version, storage driver, logging
+driver and its `max-size`, cgroup version, containers, live restore,
+whether `/etc/docker/daemon.json` exists - and what in it commonly
+causes trouble, warnings first
+([`app/services/docker_host_check.py`](https://github.com/sparkycz1/debcontrol/blob/main/app/services/docker_host_check.py)):
+
+| Finding | Level | What it means |
+|---|---|---|
+| Logs without rotation | warn | the `json-file` driver (Docker's default) without `max-size`, per container and for the daemon's default - the logs grow until the disk is full |
+| Big log files | warn | container log files over 100 MB (only when the account can read them, i.e. root) |
+| Docker Engine update | warn | a newer `docker-ce` / `docker.io` / `moby-engine` package waits (from the machine's last package check) |
+| Privileged containers | warn | `--privileged` |
+| Deprecated storage driver | warn | `devicemapper`, `aufs`, `overlay`, `vfs` |
+| Invalid `daemon.json` | warn | the daemon won't start after its next restart |
+| No memory limit | info | running containers without one |
+| Docker socket mounted | info | root on the host for whoever controls the container |
+| Host network or PID namespace | info | `--network host` / `--pid host` |
+| Live restore off | info | containers stop while the daemon restarts or is upgraded (not reported under Swarm) |
+| Docker warnings | info | what `docker info` itself warns about |
+
+Each finding says how to fix it. The check is read with every *Check
+image updates* (also *Check now* on the page) by one read-only SSH
+command
+([`app/ssh/docker_host.py`](https://github.com/sparkycz1/debcontrol/blob/main/app/ssh/docker_host.py))
+and stored on the machine (`Machine.docker_host_check`); the Containers
+page links to it when it found warnings.
+
